# Kubernetes Agent Boundaries

## Namespace Restrictions

**Allowed namespace:** `utilities`

- Deploy applications only to the `utilities` namespace
- Do not create or modify resources in other namespaces without explicit permission

## Protected Namespaces (Do Not Modify)

- `kube-system` - CoreDNS, kube-proxy, CNI
- `monitoring` - Prometheus, Grafana, AlertManager
- `default`
- `kube-public`
- `kube-node-lease`

## Confirmation Required

Ask for explicit confirmation before:

- Modifying cluster-wide resources (ClusterRole, ClusterRoleBinding, StorageClass)
- Changing DNS, networking, or ingress configurations
- Deleting any resource
- Patching ConfigMaps in system namespaces
- Rolling out restarts in non-utilities namespaces

## Allowed Operations (No Confirmation Needed)

- Read/list resources in any namespace
- Create/update resources in `utilities` namespace
- Port-forward to services
- View logs and describe resources

## Example

```bash
# ✅ Allowed
kubectl apply -f manifest.yaml -n utilities
kubectl delete pod my-pod -n utilities

# ❌ Not allowed without asking
kubectl patch cm coredns -n kube-system ...
kubectl delete deployment -n monitoring ...
```
